{"id": "EUVD-2026-30889", "enisaUuid": "2c0b12eb-9872-3e6b-b856-435ec45f7cec", "description": "A session fixation vulnerability was found in Keycloak's login-actions endpoints. An unauthenticated attacker could exploit this flaw by pre-creating an authentication session and tricking a victim into visiting a maliciously crafted link. By leveraging the /login-actions/restart endpoint\u2014which processes session handles without adequate CSRF protection or cookie ownership validation\u2014an attacker can reset the authentication flow state. This causes Single Sign-On (SSO) to authenticate the victim transparently upon clicking the link, allowing the attacker to hijack the required-action form without needing the victim's credentials. A successful exploit could lead to complete account takeover, including highly privileged administrative accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-05-19T11:01:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T16:59:00", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19594", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19595", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19596", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19597", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76128", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76129", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76130", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76132", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:76134", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-7507", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2464145"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-7507", "GHSA-hf67-5vvq-fm3r"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 1.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0088f347-6abb-3a32-9215-440783547b0f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6 for RHEL 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:18.0.20-1.redhat_00001.1.el8sso"}, {"id": "4df4d2fa-b3b4-3ad7-a6a5-7846c1f06389", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6 for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:18.0.20-1.redhat_00001.1.el9sso"}, {"id": "54bd465a-583e-32df-8342-b15150448cde", "product": {"name": "Red Hat build of Keycloak 26.2", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 26.2.16-1"}, {"id": "646edaeb-4a12-3a7e-9473-45435d5f217c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat build of Keycloak 26.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 26.4.12-1"}, {"id": "7e4d331c-9811-3522-aec2-4af4eb300cd2", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6 for RHEL 7", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:18.0.20-1.redhat_00001.1.el7sso"}, {"id": "7f3f8eda-cbca-3ea4-ae09-00aa65a327aa", "product": {"name": "RHEL-8 based Middleware Containers", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.6-85"}, {"id": "9c2c3a2e-a8dc-3161-9d24-75caa7d4ac54", "product": {"name": "Red Hat build of Keycloak 26.2", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 26.2-21"}, {"id": "fac6de28-ed04-31e2-8c3b-d3086f0c7d55", "product": {"name": "Red Hat build of Keycloak 26.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 26.4-17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fb707069-5ba0-367d-9d27-ef27d84abda0", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}